  "chapter": {
    "number": 104,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(105) Alleluia."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Give thanks to the Lord, and call upon his name; declare his works among the heathen.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sing to him, yes, sing praises to him: tell forth all his wonderful works.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Glory in his holy name: let the heart of them that seek the Lord rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Seek you⌃ the Lord, and be strengthened; seek his face continually.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember his wonderful works that he has done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "you⌃ seed of Abraam, his servants, you⌃ children of Jacob, his chosen ones.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He is the Lord our God; his judgments are in all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has remembered his covenant for ever, the word which he commanded for a thousand generation:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "which he established as a covenant to Abraam, and he remembered his oath to Isaac.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he established it to Jacob for an ordinance, and to Israel for an everlasting covenant;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "saying To you will I give the land of Chanaan, the line of your inheritance:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "when they were few in number, very few, and sojourners in it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they went from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He suffered no man to wrong them; and he rebuked kings for their sakes:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "saying, Touch not my anointed ones; and do my prophets no harm.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Moreover he called for a famine upon the land; he broke the whole support of bread.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent a man before them; Joseph was sold for a slave.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 195
          },
          {
            "text": "hurt his feet with fetters;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 196
          },
          {
            "text": "his soul passed into iron,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "until the time that his cause came on; the word of the Lord tried him as fire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The king sent and loosed him; even the prince of the people, and let him go free.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He made him Lord over his house, and ruler of all his substance;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to chastise his rulers at his pleasure, and to teach his elders wisdom.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Israel also came into Egypt, and Jacob sojourned in the land of Cham.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he increased his people greatly, and made them stronger than their enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he turned their heart to hate his people, to deal craftily with his servants.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent forth Moses his servant, and Aaron whom he had chosen.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He established among them his signs, and his wonders in the land of Cham.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent forth darkness, and made it dark; yet they",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 197
          },
          {
            "text": "rebelled against his words.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He turned their waters into blood, and killed their fish.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Their land produced frogs abundantly, in the chambers of their kings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He spoke, and the dog-fly came, and lice in all their coasts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 32,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He turned their rain into hail, and sent flaming fire in their land.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 33,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he struck their vines and their fig trees; and broke every tree of their coast.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 34,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He spoke, and the locust came, and caterpillars innumerable,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 35,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and devoured all the grass in their land, and devoured the fruit of the ground.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 36,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He struck also every firstborn of their land, the first fruits of all their labor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 37,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he brought them out with silver and gold; and there was not a feeble one among their tribes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 38,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Egypt rejoiced at their departing; for the fear of them fell upon them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 39,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He spread out a cloud for a covering to them, and fire to give them light by night.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 40,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They asked, and the quail came, and he satisfied them with the bread of heaven.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 41,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He clave the rock, and the waters flowed, rivers ran in dry places.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 42,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he remembered his holy word, which he promised to Abraam his servant.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 43,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he brought out his people with exultation, and his chosen with joy;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 44,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and gave them the lands of the heathen; and they inherited the labors of the people;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 45,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "that they might keep his ordinances, and diligently seek his law.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 195,
        "caller": "+",
